comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-05T07:30:20.705Z",codex-sol,"Plan: inspect SDK tracker discovery and runtime fence exports; apply non-negatable runtime exclusions to status and staging. Replace narrow staging acceptance with real priority/tags updates and unrestricted add across served clones."
  "2026-10-05T07:49:26.769Z",codex-sol,"SDK exports getPmGitignoreBlock, so no copied path list or hardcoded tracker root is needed. Real priority/tags updates with unrestricted stage now converge with zero conflicts and verify clean on all three stores. Custom tracker tests also cover non-negatable fences, external PM_PATH and preserved search/eval-queries.json."
  "2026-10-05T07:58:19.741Z",codex-sol,"Custom tracker and legacy-index regressions pass. SDK search/* fence patterns are widened to cover descendants, matching Git directory-ignore semantics, while the curated eval-queries.json exception remains trackable. Strict pm health passes."
  "2026-10-05T08:01:30.777Z",codex-sol,"Linked runtime acceptance passes 14/14 with zero skips: real priority/tags mutations, unrestricted add, zero merge conflicts, clean server/clone verification, custom SDK tracker discovery, nested search-cache exclusions, curated search evidence preservation and legacy index removal. Updated the older empty-ignore expectation to include the new runtime fence without weakening the unreadable-file check."
  "2026-10-05T08:16:03.640Z",codex-sol,"At 058a66b the npm release run passes all 842 tests with no skips, but its 100-percent branch gate identifies one missing branch. Review confirmed that the SDK fence reused isIgnored and thereby included the global ignore list, misclassifying Git control files as PM runtime state in explicit-add guidance. Separated fence pattern matching from global exclusions and added assertions for the distinction; all gates will be rerun."
